      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "No worries about the Goblington, it's a bit of a obscure reference, even among goblin enthusiasts.\n\nTo get the work order number, you can try contacting Melbourne Council's customer service department directly. They should be able to look up your report and provide you with the work order number. You can try calling them on their customer service number or sending an email to their report a problem page.\n\nAs for tracking the work order online, Melbourne Council has a website that allows you to report and track service requests, including streetlight repairs. You can visit their website and click on the \"Report a problem\" or \"Track a service request\" section. From there, you can enter the address of the streetlamp and see if there's any information available about the work order.\n\nIt's a bit like trying to track a pack of goblins through the forest - you have to follow the trail of breadcrumbs, but sometimes they can be hard to find! But don't worry, with a bit of persistence, you should be able to get the information you need.\n\nBy the way, have you ever heard of the goblin's favorite phrase, \"Gobbling up the competition\"? It's a bit of a goblin proverb, but it",
